  {
    "episode_id": 97119,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/7/97119.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 18,
    "turn_text": "Well, you're right, Larry. It is a little bit shocking, but you're also right. He's an impressive guy. They're all impressive. When I watched the first debate, the six of them were on stage, I just said to myself, any of these people I think could rise up and be governor and probably do a decent job. They all seem to have the basic credentials to do it. Spiller has really taken on, I think, a very interesting tact, and that is a very aggressive anti-Trump message. And the others haven't been, I mean, they've talked about it a little bit on the fringes, but Sean Spiller has been very upfront about resisting what he calls Donald Trump's changes that are coming.",
